@gwern Don’t overrotate on my initial use of the word “style”.

By using the artists name in the prompt, you’re invariably going to use IP that belongs to the artist. Maybe not every generation, but most of them. 

You can’t possibly want artists to get disenfranchised by generative AI?

@gwern Fashion is a specific edge case, not the norm from an IP perspective.

Mickey Mouse is owned &amp; enforceable IP, and I’ll pay to have Mickey Mouse in legal content I want to produce.

I also think 0-marginal-cost content generation is weird &amp; unprecedented, so analogies don’t hold.

